OL,3,GNEWSAButterfly populations 'could
OL,4,Acrash' due to weather
OL,5,
OL,6,FButterfly and day-flying moth numbers
OL,7,Frecorded across Devon and Cornwall this
OL,8,Fsummer have been "very good" - but
OL,9,Fexperts fear prolonged hot and dry
OL,10,Fweather could lead to a decline.
OL,12,FNearly 5,000 people took part in the
OL,13,FButterfly Conservation's 2026 big
OL,14,Fbutterfly count in Devon, recording
OL,15,F77,151 insects during the three-week
OL,16,Fcount. It said nearly 3,000 people took
OL,17,Fpart in Cornwall, spotting 47,712.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,344,340,200,160,0,100
