OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F343A1790421955
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSAButterfly populations 'could
OL,4,Acrash' due to weather
OL,5,
OL,6,FHead of science at the conservation,
OL,7,Fprofessor Richard Fox, said adult
OL,8,Fbutterflies loved hot weather, but
OL,9,Fwarned we could be on course "for a
OL,10,Fpopulation crash".
OL,12,F"The extreme droughts in 1976 and 1995
OL,13,Fhad severe impacts on butterfly
OL,14,Fpopulations, with some species never
OL,15,Ffully recovering," he said.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
